2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229658 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229658 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$ \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by substitution from lines {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229658 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2c2234c8-1637-5807-8336-81efdf9ec90b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229658 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is a fundamental matrix, every solution of the system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c\\,\\text{for some constant vector }c.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{properties of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Evaluating the identity $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ at $t=0$ gives \n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{evaluating both sides at }t=0.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ from $\\text{L1}$ and $c=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and substitution from $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229677 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229677 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335023" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229677 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229677 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229677 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "56cd9daa-00e7-5df3-81ab-61efadc99e76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229677 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230002 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186230003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230002 #edb/ref 1061 592270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230002 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c774d65b-c500-58e4-aa9a-e222d3d136ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230002 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186230188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230003 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186230004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230003 #edb/ref 1061 592271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230003 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d3b52974-38d7-50fa-b648-b51510a9a617" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230003 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186229142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230004 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186230005 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230004 #edb/ref 1061 592274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230004 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5206e604-fe74-5b8a-800c-cdb747dc1e28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230004 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186230193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230005 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186230006 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230005 #edb/ref 1061 592275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230005 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c93fbf09-3c42-5a66-8e76-1cf0d810f44a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230005 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186229143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230006 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186230007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230006 #edb/ref 1061 592278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230006 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "19b34f7c-755c-5e1b-a16f-22bd17d1ecc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230006 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186230194 #edb/ref 17592