egin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311563 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c88de0a-b8a5-5d49-8f68-2a26f0c469ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311563 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5t} & t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5t} & t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186310977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311590 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335429" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311590 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311590 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(4) \\\\ y(4)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & t{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"100px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311590 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7467b4a4-4b5f-508d-a258-892c78866514" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311590 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-4)}\\,x(4) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t-4} & (t-4){e}^{t-4} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t-4}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,(5-t){e}^{t-4}\\, \\\\ \\,-{e}^{t-4}\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311591 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311591 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311591 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335430" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311591 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311591 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=7x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=7y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(-3) \\\\ y(-3)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{7t} & t{e}^{7t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{7t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"140px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311591 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "467988d5-2a79-550a-9715-201ca6f86285" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311591 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t+3)}\\,x(-3) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{7(t+3)} & (t+3){e}^{7(t+3)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{7(t+3)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,(-2t-6){e}^{7(t+3)}\\, \\\\ \\,-2{e}^{7(t+3)}\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311592 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186310951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311592 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311592 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335437" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311592 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311592 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=8y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-8x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(-1) \\\\ y(-1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311592 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b7870a76-0c90-529a-9ddb-a95d0acab0af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311592 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t+1)}\\,x(-1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8(t+1)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8(t+1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8(t+1)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8(t+1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8(t+1))\\, \\\\ \\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8(t+1))\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311593 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311593 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335449" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311593 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311593 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(2) \\\\ y(2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311593 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "55bee6bc-3983-5e41-8e4f-3cb5fd416427" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311593 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-2)}\\,x(2) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311799 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186310956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311799 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311799 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311799 #edb/ref 1069 "q-337115" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311799 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311799 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L8}$ by the fact that {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311799 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0ff7b45c-b6c0-5a02-9a69-d827819f7539" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311799 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Line $\\text{L5}$ gives\n\n$$\n({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c.\n$$\n\nSince $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}={I}_{n}$, the right-hand side simplifies to $c$, so\n\n$$\nc=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nSimplify once, then apply $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$, to obtain\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L6}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L7}.$ Using line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c.\n$$\n\nFrom line $\\text{L6}$, we know that $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}).$ Substituting this expression for $c$ into the formula for $x(t)$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L7}.$ Thus, line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by $\\text{substituting }c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\text{ into }x(t)={e}^{At}c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L8}$ and $\\text{L9}.$ Starting from $\\text{L8},$\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwe rewrite the exponent using the algebraic identity $At-A{t}_{0}=A(t-{t}_{0})$ to get\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L9}.$ Thus, $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L8}$ by the fact that $At-A{t}_{0}=A(t-{t}_{0})\\text{ for any }t\\text{ and }{t}_{0}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372648 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372648 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372648 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372648 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372652 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372648 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372648 #edb/ref 1077 "field-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372648 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186372650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372648 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ab481dec-1ae8-51be-b85b-70941d4f372